Package: dmdprices
Title: Look Up Medicine Prices from the NHS dm+d
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person("Will", "Hardy", email = "w.hardy@bangor.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Programmatic tools to look up, optimise, and cost NHS medicine
    prices from the bundled dm+d (Dictionary of Medicines and Devices) pricing
    dataset (Week 15 2026). Query Drug Tariff and NHS Indicative Prices by
    medicine name (partial, exact, or fuzzy), find the cheapest or fewest-pack
    combination that delivers a dose, and adjust costs between years with the
    NHS Cost Inflation Index. Also loads updated releases from the NHSBSA
    'dmdDataLoader' CSV output. Prices are derived from dm+d; output columns
    mirror the NHS Drug Tariff Part VIIIA CSV format for interoperability. The
    dm+d data is Crown copyright, licensed under the Open Government Licence
    v3.0
    <https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/>.
